## Code rules

- Follow the existing pattern. Before you design something new, find how the repo solves the same problem and match it. If you diverge, say why.
- Never hardcode a value that a contract, an enum, a config or an API response gives. Import it.
- After you fix a defect, search sibling code for the same defect, and fix it or report it.
- Doc comments on public functions, in ASD-STE100.
- @@PACKAGE_RULE@@
- No secrets in code, config fallbacks or fixtures.

## Plans

- Plans live in `.plans/`, named `YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-<kebab-slug>.md`. Finished plans move to `.plans/done/`.
- Validation reports live in `.plans/.validations/`. Run reports live in `.plans/auto-runs/` (gitignored).
- `@@PARENT_PLAN@@` is the parent plan. Child plans are written one step ahead.
- A big piece of work that needs several plans has its own parent plan: `.plans/YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-<slug>-parent.md`, which starts with `> **Master plan.**` (no steps, never launched) and holds the ordered child plans, the owner's decisions and the open decisions. `@@PARENT_PLAN@@` links each parent plan. A child plan names its parent plan in its header (`- **Parent**:`).
- Every plan starts only after an explicit "go" from the owner, or when the plans dashboard starts it because the `- **Waits for**:` condition in its header became true (that line is the go). One plan per run.
- When a plan needs an owner decision, do not guess. Write the question down and continue with the steps that do not depend on it.

## Workflow

`/skill-1-plan <what>` (writes the plan, then validates it) → push the plan to `@@BASE_BRANCH@@` → launch it in the plans dashboard → review the draft PR → merge → `bash .claude/scripts/auto-pipeline.sh --cleanup <slug>`.

- `/skill-1-plan` asks the owner one decision at a time, saves `.plans/<file>.md`, then runs `/skill-auto-validate-plan`.
@@IF MOD_CODEX@@
- `/skill-auto-validate-plan` loops (max 2 rounds): the `plan-validator` agent and Codex (when `codex` is installed) each write a report in `.plans/.validations/`, the valid findings go into the plan, and each round leaves a `-round-<n>.md` decision log. `/skill-validate-plan` is one Claude round with no edits.
@@END@@
@@IFNOT MOD_CODEX@@
- `/skill-auto-validate-plan` loops (max 2 rounds): the `plan-validator` agent writes `.plans/.validations/<plan-basename>-validation-<n>.md`, the valid findings go into the plan, and each round leaves a `-round-<n>.md` decision log. `/skill-validate-plan` is one round with no edits.
@@END@@
- `/apply-validation` checks a pasted review (another agent, another session, a person) against the repo and writes `-external-<n>.md`.
- The dashboard runs `.claude/scripts/auto-pipeline.sh <mode> <plan>`. It creates a worktree `../worktrees/@@PROJECT_NAME@@/<slug>` on branch `auto/<slug>` from `origin/@@BASE_BRANCH@@` and runs `/skill-auto-pipeline` headless: @@PIPELINE_CHAIN@@. Modes: stop at verify (nothing committed), full (one local commit), to PR. The report is `.plans/auto-runs/<slug>.md`.
- `/skill-2-implement <plan file>` alone implements one plan in the current tree, with no commits.
- `/skill-3-test` and `/skill-4-verify` also run alone, after a manual `/skill-2-implement`.
@@IF CODEX_IN_VERIFY@@
- `/skill-4-verify` runs a review loop of max 2 rounds, each round one Claude `/code-review` and then one Codex review (`.codex/skills/validate-implementation`, when `codex` is installed; `--no-codex` skips it), then the rule audit. A missing Codex never blocks it.
@@END@@
@@IFNOT CODEX_IN_VERIFY@@
- `/skill-4-verify` runs a `/code-review` loop of max 2 rounds (round 2 only after a behaviour fix), then the rule audit.
@@END@@
- `/skill-5-ship` merges `@@BASE_BRANCH@@`, runs the checks, pushes the branch and opens a draft PR. Only when the owner asks.
@@IF HAS_REVIEW_GATE@@
- **Board:** `/skill-5-ship` moves a ticket to "@@BOARD_STATUS@@" only when every "Done when" line is in a PR (also the parts in other repos); a partial PR leaves the Status as it is. After a release to `@@STAGING_BRANCH@@`, `/staging-review` moves each ticket whose PRs are all on `@@STAGING_BRANCH@@` to "@@BOARD_REVIEW_STATUS@@", with the staging versions in a comment. QA works only on "@@BOARD_REVIEW_STATUS@@".
@@END@@
@@IF MOD_TEST_REVIEW@@
- `/test-review` checks the tests of a change against the plan (the `test-reviewer` agent). The pipeline runs it inside `/skill-4-verify`.
@@END@@
@@IF MOD_CHANGELOG@@
- `/changelog-entry` writes the `changelog.d/` entry of a change. Every PR adds one, or carries the `no-changelog` label.
@@END@@
@@IF MOD_DECISION_SHEET@@
- `/decision-sheet` writes the decisions of a change for the reviewer. In "to PR" mode the pipeline runs it before the commit (its fixes go into the one commit); `/skill-5-ship` adds it to the PR.
@@END@@
@@IF MOD_PLANS_PARALLEL@@
- `/plans-parallel` reads `node .claude/scripts/plan-lanes.mjs --json` and proposes which plans can run at the same time.
@@END@@
@@IF MOD_PR_FEEDBACK@@
- `/pr-feedback <PR>` works the review comments of a PR in its run worktree.
@@END@@
- The skill names are a contract with the plans dashboard (it looks for `/skill-auto-pipeline <slug>.md` to see a live run, and copies `/skill-auto-validate-plan`). Do not rename them.
- Every skill runs shell commands bare: one command per call, no pipes, `&&`, redirection or heredocs. Headless runs auto-deny compound commands.

## Git

- Branches: @@BRANCH_CHAIN@@. `@@BASE_BRANCH@@` is the base branch. PRs go to `@@BASE_BRANCH@@`.
- Never wait for or watch GitHub CI runs (no `gh pr checks --watch`, no polling). After a push the step is done.
- Push only when the owner says so, or as a follow-up on an open PR (next rule). The "to PR" mode counts as that permission, for its own `auto/<slug>` branch only. Never push @@PROTECTED_BRANCHES@@ from an automated run. Never force-push.
- **Follow-ups on an open PR: commit and push without asking.** When the current branch is not @@PROTECTED_BRANCHES@@ and has an open PR (`gh pr view --json number,state` says `OPEN`), each change the owner asks for in the chat ships to that PR. Do not hand over `git add` or `git commit` commands. Run the scoped tests and the check-only lint for the touched files; a failure → fix it or report it, and do not push. Stage by path (never `git add -A` or `git add .`; never `.env*`, `.claude/settings.local.json` or the files of another plan), commit with a Conventional Commits message, and `git push`. When the change makes the PR body wrong (Changes, Verification, Code review, Open points), update the body with `gh pr edit <number> --body-file <file>`. This rule overrides a personal "never commit unless asked" rule for this case only.
- Merge style: @@MERGE_STYLE@@ (@@MERGE_HINT@@).
- Commit messages use Conventional Commits, with no AI attribution.

